    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) headline our offensive assault against a vulnerable matchup, both benefiting from a significant park factor boost and a favorable encounter with Littell. **Ward**\u2019s role at the top of the order adds a valuable 10% premium to his projection, making him our highest-ceiling asset despite a 30% rain risk. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) provides exceptional utility value; his xwOBA of .374 and the dynamic platoon edge against Kelly allow him to punch well above his base projection. We are also capitalizing on **Daulton Varsho** (66.20), whose 91% SB profile against a slow delivery from Rocker makes him an essential start given our team-wide prioritization of stolen base efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Arraez** (42.62), who nearly cracked the lineup for his reliability but ultimately lost out due to the formidable presence of Chris Sale on the mound. Sale\u2019s 3.01 xERA acted as a significant anchor, dragging **Arraez**\u2019s score below our optimal threshold for active play. While we considered slotting him in for the high-volume lineup spot, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of **Tyler Freeman** and **Lawrence Butler** against their respective left-handed matchups. We will keep **Arraez**, along with **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Drew Gilbert**, in reserve to monitor potential late-game pinch-hit scenarios, though we are wary of the weather volatility surrounding **Ward** and **Beavers**\u2014if those games are delayed, we may need to pivot to our bench depth quickly to preserve our game caps.",
